    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Every morning, find the ones who went quiet\nA lead that nobody followed up is the most expensive thing a sales\nteam owns \u2014 it cost money to acquire and returns nothing. This runs\ndaily and works out who is due a nudge, using two queries rather\nthan one per person, so it stays well inside the CRM's rate limit.",
        "height": 320,
        "width": 640,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "683371836386",
      "name": "1. Every morning, find the ones who went quiet",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -20,
        140
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Decide who is due, and stop when you should\nDay 3, day 7, day 14 \u2014 then never again. It stops early if they\nreplied, if they opted out, or if they already became a real\nopportunity. A sequence that does not know how to stop is how\ncompanies end up in spam folders.",
        "height": 380,
        "width": 540,
        "color": 6
      },
      "id": "798455399991",
      "name": "2. Decide who is due, and stop when you should",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        640,
        80
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Send it the only way anything can be sent\nEach nudge goes through the send sub-workflow, so the consent gate\napplies exactly as it does everywhere else. Someone who opted out\nyesterday is refused here today, without this workflow needing to\nknow the rule.",
        "height": 320,
        "width": 640,
        "color": 2
      },
      "id": "611570152186",
      "name": "3. Send it the only way anything can be sent",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1200,
        140
      ]
    }
